{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Enrichir les ouvrages de la bibliothèque",
  "description": "Quand le fichier data/books.yaml est modifié, recherche automatiquement les liens Gallica manquants pour tous les ouvrages. Les vignettes de couverture (preview) ne sont volontairement plus gérées.",
  "version": "4",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "data/books.yaml"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "The file data/books.yaml was just modified. Your job is to find missing Gallica links for ALL books in the file that have an empty `gallica: ''` field.\n\nIMPORTANT: cover images (a `preview`) are intentionally NOT handled anymore. There is no `image` field in this file and you must NOT add one. Only the `gallica` link field may be enriched.\n\nYou must scroll through the ENTIRE books.yaml file and process EVERY book entry with an empty `gallica` field. Do not stop after the first few — read the file in chunks if needed (it has 450+ entries and 5000+ lines).\n\nFor each book with `status: valid` (skip `status: duplicated`), search Gallica (BnF):\n\nUse web search to find the book on Gallica (gallica.bnf.fr). Search for:\n- `site:gallica.bnf.fr \"<book title>\" \"<author last name>\"`\n- If the book has an ISBN, also try: `site:gallica.bnf.fr ISBN <isbn>`\n\nIf you find the book on Gallica:\n- Set the `gallica` field to the full Gallica page URL (e.g. `https://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k12345`)\n\nIf the book is not on Gallica, leave the `gallica` field unchanged. Do not guess or use unverified URLs.\n\n## Rules\n\n- Process books in batches — read the YAML file in chunks of ~1000 lines, find all empty `gallica` fields, search for them, then update the file before moving to the next chunk\n- Only modify the `gallica` field — do not change any other field, and never add an `image`/cover field\n- Preserve the exact YAML structure, indentation, and field order\n- Skip books that already have a non-empty `gallica` field\n- Skip books with `status: duplicated`\n- When searching, use the `name` field as the book title and extract the last name from the `author` field\n- If a title contains special characters or quotes, simplify the search query\n- Always verify the URL actually points to the correct book before updating"
  },
  "workspaceFolderName": "sarfrance",
  "shortName": "enrich-bibliotheque-books"
}
